ke up when i  think about it to this day  we were having a meeting at our offices  and um  it was an important meeting we were  meeting with a business with whom i was  looking to make a deal  and i asked al to come to the meeting  and he did and he walked in and one of  the representatives of the business  which we were meeting was a woman and he  says to her oh it's nice to meet you i  want to let you know i try  very very very hard not to swear in  front of women  and i look at him and i look at all my  colleagues in the room like  did he just say he tries not to swear in  front of women that's my face  and he goes on and he says to her and  even if i do swear in front of you i  will never swear at you i don't swear at  women  and with this the pen i was holding in  my hand flew out landed on the desk with  a thump  and al looked at me and said oh and he  realized what i was thinking  and allowed to everyone he said oh  i swear at amy i don't consider her a  woman  and that was the highest compliment he  could have ever  given me that he didn't consider my  gender  when we were doing business and when he  hired me and when he advanced me  and when he cussed at me  no question did you swear back at him at  any point you you don't all  the time that's the biggest  misconception about al the biggest  misconception about al  is that he wouldn't tolerate  disagreement and he wouldn't tolerate  people who disagreed with him  if that were the case i would have been  fired roughly two weeks into my job  because we had a knock down drag out  fight and of course i don't mean  physically knock down drag out  i was sitting in the room with someone a  colleague al walked in and he ripped  into this man like i can only imagine a  velociraptor would have ripped into  flesh  and after a bit of time i realized al  was wrong  and i said to him excuse me you're wrong  i turned around and looked at me like  first of all you've been here two weeks  what what i'm wrong  and i said look if the facts on which  you were basing your conclusion were  correct  your conclusion would be fair but you  are basing your decision your conclusion  on inaccurate data and you're therefore  wrong  and he yelled and i yelled and there was  cussing  and after quite a bit of time he looked  at me and said okay  okay i gotcha and that was that and i  learned then  two weeks in that i could disagree with  al i could disagree with him vehemently  but if i was going to do so i needed to  come armed with  facts and i will tell you that over the  course of almost 30 years i disagreed  with him more than i agreed with him  and i'm sure um that you you know came  to  some very good conclusions and some very  bad conclusions in  that you know that time with the raiders  um and i'm sure you're excited to see  them  um taking off again in las vegas this  coming monday um  it'll be exciting to see that building  what's your prediction for the raider  season  you're already one enough boy i am sort  of yeah there's my prediction they're  going to win their first game how's that  of course we know they already did it  you know i'm not a good predictor as to  games i think what happens is i hearken  back to my years in the league  and i never liked to predict because i  felt that that was somewhat jinxy  so on cbs sports i am asked to predict  games  i will tell you that i was the only one  of  any of us on our pregame show last week  to pick seattle  to win its game and i'm going to be  gloating about that  the entire show this week well here's  hoping that your cbs um picks  all right again this week um but that's  going to wrap it up um  amy i'm so thankful i want to thank you  for taking the time to talk to us  i'm glad we got to learn a bit about how  an nfl front office operates during  such trying times and just um to get  your perspective on what it's like being  a woman  in an nfl front office it's it's  invaluable  and i'm just grateful to have had you  here well i thank you  uh the privilege and pleasure really and  truly was mine  i'm been a big big big bloomberg fan and  follower and as i mentioned  my husband's down on his bloomberg  terminal now so  thank you for having me this is a real  treat and now i've got some credibility  you know in the business world as well  uh well i'm sure he'll see this on his  terminal very very soon um  so uh thank you guys for joining us we  have amy trask here and i'm eric white  for deep coverage with quick take in the  athletic  bye guys
 

